---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { legalCompany, legalMailto } from "../lib/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Cookie Policy — Zenguy"
  description="Cookie policy for Zenguy under article 22.2 LSSI-CE and AEPD guidance."
  heading="Cookie Policy"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {legalCompany.legalName} uses cookies and similar
    technologies on {legalCompany.site} and {legalCompany.app}, under article
    22.2 of Law 34/2002 (LSSI-CE), the ePrivacy Directive, the GDPR, and the
    AEPD cookie guidance.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files stored on your device. Similar technologies
    include local storage, session tokens and pixels. Some are set by us
    (first-party), others by providers (third-party).
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we use today</h2>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> use advertising cookies, social plugins, or
    analytics cookies such as Google Analytics.
  </p>
  <p>
    On the application ({legalCompany.app}) we use a strictly necessary
    HttpOnly session cookie (a host-prefixed refresh token) so you stay signed
    in. It is first-party, Secure, and not accessible to scripts. Local
    storage may hold a short-lived access token and UI preferences. These are
    needed to provide the service you request, so they do not require prior
    consent (art. 22.2 LSSI-CE, first indent).
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, which hosts the websites, may set a security cookie (for
    example to distinguish people from bots). That cookie is used to keep the
    service available and safe.
  </p>
  <p>
    Stripe Checkout and the Stripe customer portal — which open only when you
    start or manage a payment — set their own cookies on Stripe’s domains.
    Those are Stripe’s responsibility and are needed to take payment.
  </p>
  <p>
    The public marketing site loads the Geist typeface from Google Fonts. That
    is a network request to Google, not a Zenguy analytics cookie. Google may
    process technical data such as IP address as described in Google’s
    documentation. We load the font because it is part of the site you asked
    to see.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Consent</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not currently set non-essential cookies on the marketing
    site, we do not show a consent banner there. If we later add analytics or
    advertising cookies, we will ask for opt-in consent first, with an equally
    easy reject control, in line with AEPD guidance. Pre-ticked boxes and
    “continued browsing” are not consent.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How to control cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking the
    session cookie will sign you out of the application. You can also use
    private browsing.
  </p>

  <h2>5. More information</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data involved in these technologies is described in the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions:{" "}
    <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
